    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f560d95-f0f5-4b24-a042-4f7cec5b50a6\n\nI have 2 completion options. One of them has a short info, the other one is longer. When i select the short one first, the \"Info\" title is shortened to \"...\" (probably intended). But when i then switch to the other option, it still stays as \"...\" (probably not inteded). When i do the opposite and choose the long option first, the title correctly displays \"Info\", but switching to the short info option sets the title to \"I\".\n\nExpected Behavior: The short info options title should always be shortened to \"...\", and the long info options title should always display fully.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nDefault Mini setup, i just changed the mappings for scrolling in the info plugin (but i didnt use them)\n\nAny Lsp that has very short infos, in my case Zig with ZLS",
